as boba fett temoira morrison is one of  the most feared men in the galaxy but  back home in new zealand why is he still  overshadowed by even more famous members  of his own family keep watching to find  out  temawera morrison's artistic lineage can  be traced to his uncle howard morrison a  legendary musician in new zealand whose  success in voice was so wide-reaching  that he was knighted beyond his music  which was popular across the south  pacific in asia sir howard dedicated his  time and effort to fighting for civil  rights in particular he rallied for  equal education and access for new  zealand's native maori people her enzy  on screen morrison recalled of his uncle  i remember as a young boy growing up we  were always told to stand up and make a  speech stand up and sing a song do this  and do that and when i look back he was  grooming us training us for our journey  however according to a biography of sir  howard written by his son howie jr the  relationship between uncle and nephew  might not have always been smooth  according to the road aurora daily post  the book revealed that sir howard didn't  want to share the limelight and  criticized tamura for his breakout role  in the acclaimed film once were warriors  during an interview with staff temawera  morrison recounted that after being  tapped to play famed australian rugby  coach eddie jones in the 2019 film the  brighton miracle he told director max  mannix are you sure i'm a maori from  rotorua new zealand the maori are  thought to have arrived in new zealand  about a thousand years ago as members of  the polynesian peoples whose ocean going  exploits are epic and as a maori  morrison is part of a collection of  successful polynesian actors blowing  open doors on hollywood this list  includes several a-listers working today  from action stars like dwayne the rock  johnson to mass singer judge nicole  scherzinger the rise of entertainers of  polynesian descent has been a great  stride for inclusiveness  timur morrison is named after his  grandfather who was a professional rugby  player morrison told roto-roo daily post  my cousin terry tapso was born a week  after me whichever one was born first  was going to be called temawera after  our morrison grandfather grandpa  morrison was a member of the new zealand  rugby squad all blacks the perennial  kings of the rugby pitch but the team  isn't without its controversies sir  howard with his group the howard  morrison quartets memorialized one such  incident involving his dad their hit  1960 protest song by old mans and all  black is about how the team wasn't  allowed to play its maori members for a  tournament in apartheid era south africa  plenty has changed since then and the  all blacks have gained global fame for  performing at pregame haka a traditional  maori dance focused on intimidating the  opponent  the average american film goer likely  didn't have any idea who temoira  morrison was before he appeared as jango  fett and then all of jango's clones  however by the time he joined the star  wars universe he had already been  nominated for several awards and even  won a few trophies for acting work in  his native new zealand his portrayal of  jake the mus heek and the 1994 kiwi hit  once were warriors made him a household  name back home but during an interview  with stuff morrison revealed that the  fame he earned through that project  wasn't everything it was cracked up to  be describing the role as a quote  millstone around his neck and expressing  displeasure with the making of the film  it was a lot of hard work and emotional  mayhem people go nutty doing movies like  that it was full on and we never knew  how it was going to turn out the hard  work paid off however as morrison won a  new zealand film and tv award for best  performance and dramatic role for once  were warriors and would later earn a  best actor win for his reprisal of jake  in the film's sequel 1999's what becomes  of the brokenhearted  the original star wars movies had a few  instances where one actor filled the  suit while another voiced it one of  these was of course boba fett with  jeremy bullock wearing the suit and  jason wingreen delivering the voice work  for boba fett's four lines and the  empire strikes back after temoira  morrison played jango fett in body and  voice in 2002's attack of the clones it  made sense that he was tapped to play  boba fett in the mandalorian in the book  of boba fett since boba fett is a clone  of django that raised an issue though  morrison's voice is obviously different  from wind greens so in 2004 lucasfilm  brought morrison back to re-record all  of boba's lines and the empire strikes  back for future releases at least  there's only one django there's only one  django and that's me  temura morrison had long wanted to  return to the star wars universe even  saying in 2017 that he'd want to play an  older captain rex another clone of jango  fett who was introduced in the 2008  animated film clone wars of course that  led to wild speculation that morrison  might actually be able to someday  portray boba fett himself even though  fett seemingly died in the return of the  jedi a pipe dream right well that dream  came true and morrison brought the  bounty hunter back to life in the  mandalorian albeit as an older boba fett  one who survived escaping from the giant  stomach of a sarlacc after that ordeal  and the ravages of time it was  inevitable that the actor would have to  shed his rugged good looks and smooth  voice in order to portray a scarred  battle-worn older boba discussing his  role in the mandalorian morrison told  starwars.com i did rely a lot on the  makeup i spent a lot of the time sitting  in the makeup chair watching what was  being applied and then things just  started to happen organically regarding  his vocal changes morrison said i  thought every now and then he'd hit some  tonal qualities where hey he has been  scarred he has been affected internally  as well so without sounding too false i  wanted to bring a little gravel in there  to give it a bit of timbre  the united kingdom and its commonwealth  nations including new zealand still view  queen elizabeth ii as their queen  despite political independence along  those lines titles and nobility are  bestowed on new zealand citizens just  like in england in new zealand the  nation's royal honors system gives  titles and names people to various  orders and honors as his bio explains  temara morrison was named to the new  zealand order of merit for services to  drama in a 1996 queen's birthday honors  while he was named as a member there are  further levels to achieve at the top are  the titles of dame and knight the level  obtained by his uncle howard morrison  therefore also known as sir howard  perhaps knighthood is destined for  morrison if he continues to captivate  audiences with his acting chops plus  considering boba fett's signature helmet  looks like something worn by medieval  knights it appears to be his destiny  temara morrison is an imposing guy he  earned accolades for playing the violent  jake the must-he and went on to play two  of the most savage bounty hunters in the  history of the galaxy but morrison likes  to also mix things up and show his  softer side once in a while it would be  nice to play just a nice man for a  change without all the hullabaloo stuff  luckily voice acting helps with that of  course he did voice django and boba  fetts both in the films and also in  video games like the star wars  battlefront series but he also voiced  the more nurturing chief tua and moana  the disney sensation with a cast that  features an all-star ensemble of the  world's biggest polynesian actors and  actresses morrison is joined by dwayne  johnson jermaine clement ali'i cravaglio  and nicole scherzing are among others in  the hit movie given his distinctively  tough voice we can only hope he  continues to talk behind the camera as  well as in front of it  in 2009 tamara morrison penned his  autobiography from haka to hollywood  morrison told the new zealand sunday  news that he hoped that his book will  inspire others to reach for the stars  like many celebrity autobiographies it  was ghost written in this case by paul  little morrison told the new zealand  sunday news i'm just going to talk a lot  and paul is going to try and make  something out of it before moving to  auckland i used to perform  professionally in my maori culture  groups i believe there's a formula to  getting to the top and by talking in  this book i might reveal how the hawker  i got to hollywood  temawera morrison is a man of many  talents acting and voice acting are just  the tip of the iceberg while his uncle  sir howard is one of new zealand's most  popular musicians of all time morrison's  father lori was a musician as well so  it's no surprise that in 2014 morrison  released his own album tem which  features covers of classic songs his dad  and uncle liked and used to perform in  an interview with radio new zealand  morrison explained how he used to listen  to his father's records he also  mentioned that when his dad came home  from work he'd shine the old man's shoes  before his father went to perform at a  venue in auckland it's fun to imagine  the elder morrisons jamming out to  american classics and it's impressive  how good tamara covers songs ranging  from midnight special to it's not  unusual on the album morrison also had  another entertainment gig hosting his  own tv shows one of which he believes  might have inspired his record deal  morrison told stuff i think sony must  have seen my tv variety show happy hour  at 9 30 p.m on tv one i said why not do  an album his hosting career may not have  lasted long but he did get george lucas  to appear on his talk show the tem show  not bad for a simple man trying to make  his way in the galaxy thank you also for  toning me there's only been me in a  sheep called dolly i think  it's a common adage that being a child  actor does not necessarily lead to a  successful adult career luckily temara  morrison whose first on-screen  appearance was at the tender age of 11  buck the trend according to enzy on  screen he was cast as a main character  rangi in 1973's rongi's catch after  director michael forlong spotted him  performing for tourists in rotorua in  the movie he plays a kid who along with  three others pursues two escaped  convicts catherine della roach who  reviewed the film for dominion said it  was quote one of the best children's  films ever made his next credit wasn't  until 11 years later the age of 22  playing a rasta street kid on the new  zealand tv series mortimer's patch two  years later he would get recurring roles  on two other new zealand tv series  seekers and adventurer from there  morrison began that long journey to  playing jango fett and blasting onto  movie screens all over the world  temura morrison's first character to  reach a global audience was jake and  once were warriors and his performance  impressed no less than legendary  american film critic roger ebert in his  review of the film ebert wrote in temura  morrison is jake the movie finds a  leading actor as elemental charismatic  and brutal as the young marlon brando he  has instinctive star power and it's his  likability that makes the violence of  his character so shocking morrison  mentioned in a 2014 interview with  screen space that to prepare for the  film he was instructed to watch brando's  performance as stanley kowalski and a  streetcar named desire so ebert's  comparison certainly makes sense what  was unexpected though is that morrison  would end up co-starring with the  legendary brando the island of dr moreau  starred brando as the title mad  scientist in a film that got quite a few  negative reviews morrison who played man  dog hybrid as zizello told screenspace  that he left the shoot because it was  dragging on before a lawyer forced him  back still morrison finally recalls  sharing the screen with one of his idols  telling rotten tomatoes it was great to  see him work see a master work no doubt  someday an up-and-comer will say that  same thing in an interview about the  time they got to work alongside morrison  himself  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite actors are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

